In SQL Server, TRUNCATE can be rolled back inside a transaction, subject to applicable restrictions.
2. INNER JOIN, LEFT JOIN and FULL OUTER JOIN
INNER JOIN returns matching rows only. LEFT JOIN returns all left-side rows plus matches. FULL OUTER JOIN returns all
rows from both sides, matching where possible.
SELECT e.Name, d.DepartmentName
FROM Employee e INNER JOIN Department d
 ON e.DepartmentId = d.DepartmentId;
SELECT e.Name, d.DepartmentName
FROM Employee e LEFT JOIN Department d
 ON e.DepartmentId = d.DepartmentId;
SELECT e.Name, d.DepartmentName
FROM Employee e FULL OUTER JOIN Department d
